{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIPlancherelInstances","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIPlancherelInstances","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIPlancherelConditional"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.defect_closedform_plancherel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.defect_closedform_plancherel","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L211-L223","doc":"**The keystone defect cubic, grounded in genuine representation theory.** Composing\n`n144C_eq_twelve_plancherel` with `n144C_closed_form`: for any `n` with `PlancherelSnData`, the\ngenuine Plancherel squared-hook expression equals the keystone defect cubic `−n(n−1)(2n−13)`\n(cleared by `n!`).  At the registered `n = 2..12` this is therefore **unconditional** — including\nthe `n = 7` sign flip the keystone's falsifiable target hinges on.\n\n**Uncapped 2026-08-23** as `KeystoneDefectGeneral.defect_closedform_plancherel`, which needs no\ninstance and no bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.n144C_eq_twelve_plancherel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.n144C_eq_twelve_plancherel","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L200-L209","doc":"**`n144C` in terms of the genuine Plancherel sum.** For any `n` with `PlancherelSnData`,\n`n144C n · n! = 12·(Σ_λ dim(λ)²·Σ_c h_c²) − (sixS n + 12n)·n!` — the carried `twoM` `def` is\neliminated in favour of the real squared-hook sum via `twoM_eq_plancherel_hook_sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.twoM_plancherel_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.twoM_plancherel_seven","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L178-L183","doc":"Identity I, **unconditional at `n = 7`** (the defect-cubic sign-flip degree). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.twoM_plancherel_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.twoM_plancherel_six","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L171-L176","doc":"Identity I, **unconditional at `n = 6`**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.twoM_plancherel_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.twoM_plancherel_five","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L164-L169","doc":"Identity I, **unconditional at `n = 5`** (the s5-so3 keystone's own `n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.twoM_plancherel_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.twoM_plancherel_four","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L157-L162","doc":"Identity I, **unconditional at `n = 4`**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.twoM_plancherel_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.twoM_plancherel_three","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L150-L155","doc":"Identity I, **unconditional at `n = 3`** (the deuteron `pn` channel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_twelve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_twelve","kind":"instance","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L132-L140","doc":"**`PlancherelSnData 12`** — 77 partitions (`Σ dim² = 12! = 479001600`), the bound of the\nunderlying `dim_validated_le12` / `idB_verified_le12` machine checks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_eleven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_eleven","kind":"instance","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L123-L130","doc":"**`PlancherelSnData 11`** — 56 partitions (`Σ dim² = 11! = 39916800`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_ten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_ten","kind":"instance","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L114-L121","doc":"**`PlancherelSnData 10`** — 42 partitions (`Σ dim² = 10! = 3628800`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_nine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_nine","kind":"instance","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L105-L112","doc":"**`PlancherelSnData 9`** — 30 partitions (`Σ dim² = 9! = 362880`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_eight","kind":"instance","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L96-L103","doc":"**`PlancherelSnData 8`** — 22 partitions (`Σ dim² = 8! = 40320`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_seven","kind":"instance","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L82-L94","doc":"**`PlancherelSnData 7`** — the 15 partitions of 7 (`Σ dim² = 5040 = 7!`).  `n = 7` is where\nthe falsifiable defect cubic `144·C(n) = −n(n−1)(2n−13)` has its **sign flip** (`2n−13` changes\nsign), so this is the most diagnostic `n` for the keystone's defect target — Identity I is now\nproved (not axiomatic) exactly there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_six","kind":"instance","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L72-L80","doc":"**`PlancherelSnData 6`** — the 11 partitions of 6 (`Σ dim² = 720 = 6!`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_five","kind":"instance","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L61-L70","doc":"**`PlancherelSnData 5`** — the 7 partitions of 5, hook-length dimensions `1, 4, 5, 6, 5, 4, 1`\n(`Σ dim² = 1+16+25+36+25+16+1 = 120 = 5!`).  `n = 5` is the s5-so3 keystone's own degree\n(`S₅ ⊃ A₅ ≅ I ⊂ SO(3)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.plancherelSnData_three","kind":"instance","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IdentityIPlancherelInstances.lean#L50-L59","doc":"**`PlancherelSnData 3`** — partitions `[3], [2,1], [1,1,1]` with hook-length dimensions\n`1, 2, 1`.  (i) `Σ dim² = 1+4+1 = 6 = 3!`; (ii) `2·Σ dim²·Σc² = 2·(1·5+4·2+1·5) = 36 = 3·2·3!`.\n`n = 3` is the deuteron `pn` channel of the keystone's binding-side target. ","signatureChunk":0}]}